// name :
"P1378543754" "Collateral Damage"
// flashbackteamrequiresfailedtext :
"P1137444542" "You and everyone on your team must be at least level 25 and cannot be partway through Laura Lockhart's storyarc in order to start this arc."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - LauraLockhartSouvenir 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P4252716230" "United Nations Special Service Medal"
// tDetailString :
"P2894337555" "Colonel Taggard pinned this on you personally, in honor of your efforts against the 5th Column. The memory is tinged with regret, however, and you remember the struggle as a desperate campaign against...<br><br><color gold><b>Collateral Damage</color></b><br><br>It began when Petty Officer Laura Lockhart of the United Nations Special Forces contacted you about a recent problem with the 5th Column. For some reason, the Column had become increasingly bold in their attacks on Council outposts, and the fighting was spilling out into Steel Canyon proper. She recruited two heroes to help her with the growing 5th Column threat: you, and another Paragon native named Leon.<br><br>You and Leon worked together to fight back the 5th Column. Your mission was to gather information regarding the source of the 5th Column surge - a mission that seemed to run into repeated dead ends. Only when Laura sent you on a solo mission to identify a secretive Column informant did you begin to make headway in your task.<br><br>Unfortunately, as soon as you began making progress against the Column, their informant gave up information on the Steel Canyon UNSF headquarters. The 5th Column sent a full invasion force, and you had to rush to their defense. Laura perished in the struggle, and the informant revealed his true motives - Leon himself had been working with the 5th Column from the beginning.<br><br>You managed to drive off an overwhelming force of 5th Column soldiers, and left to pursue Leon. During your final confrontation, you were faced with Leon and a 5th Column Commander, working together against the Council. By breaking the Column's connection with their new source of information, you managed to stop their surge into Steel Canyon... but at great cost."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - FlashbackLeft 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LeonTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P3791492722" "<color orange>Leon glares at you irritably.</color><br><br>As I'm sure you've overheard, I have this situation under control. I've taken out their commander, and most of the base's defenses. I doubt the remaining troops will put up much resistance.<br><br><color orange>Leon sighs.</color><br><br>But, I suppose having someone to watch my back isn't so bad. I'm Leon. What do I call you?"
// Answer Text :
"P640933230" "{HeroName} is fine."
// Answer Text :
"P258312989" "Oh, don't worry about me. I'm just some lowly *novice*, hardly worth your attention."
// Page Friendly Text :
"P3923515738" "Right. Well, {HeroName}, there's not much more for us here. The facility itself has been crippled, but they managed to completely wipe their database before I could stop them.<br><br>At this point, I don't think we're going to get any valuable info from this place. I recommend we withdraw and search elsewhere."
// Answer Text :
"P531325636" "We could bring their Commander in for interrogation..."
// Page Friendly2 Text :
"P3792489917" "He's not in any shape to be answering questions, {HeroName}, and neither are his troops. If you catch my meaning.<br><br><color orange>Leon's face goes hard, and he gestures to the motionless body of the nearby commander."
// Answer Text :
"P2901394730" "Yes, I see. That's... unfortunate."
// Page Friendly3 Text :
"P3328958422" "<color orange>You hear muffled shouting from the direction you came. It sounds like the Column is getting reinforcements of their own.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P749030525" "I think it's time we let ourselves out."
// Page Abrasive Text :
"P3776117013" "<color orange>Leon scowls at you.</color><br><br>No need to get your tights in a bind, pal. I told Lockhart that I have the situation under control, and I do. As you can plainly see.<br><br><color orange>Leon gestures to the motionless body of the nearby commander."
// Answer Text :
"P3352955166" "And I suppose you have the data we need as well?"
// Page Abrasive2 Text :
"P3794613447" "That data was wiped long before I got here. I know what I'm doing, and I <i>don't</i> need you hounding my tail, trying to second-guess me.<br><br>Look, I can't stop you from tagging along on this counterintelligence goose chase but I sure don't have to put up with you interfering with my work."
// Answer Text :
"P1807694320" "No, it looks like you failed this mission just fine on your own."
// Page Abrasive3 Text :
"P3310430230" "<color orange>Leon's eyes flare at your remark. He opens his mouth to say something, but thinks better of it.<br><br>You hear muffled shouting from the direction you came. It sounds like the Column is getting reinforcements of their own."
// Answer Text :
"P3204071113" "Time for us to leave. Try to keep up."
// Page NotOwner Text :
"P1932878120" "<color skyblue>Only the team leader can cause the mission to progress though dialogue."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2344235270" "Alright. The first thing we need to do is to try to get a bead on what, exactly, is causing the 5th Column to become so active in this region.<br><br>My intel team has been tracking their comm traffic, but it's encrypted. We can't figure out what they're saying, but we CAN figure out who's talking to whom - and we've located a hub of recent activity.<br><br>If we can get our hands on their encryption codes, we might be able to get the inside info we need."
// AcceptString :
"P275517837" "I'm guessing that's where I come in."
// SendOffString :
"P2412987149" "Well, sort of. I've already made the recommendation to another local hero recruit, goes by the name Leon. He's got an infiltration mission underway.<br><br>I <i>think</i> he can handle himself in there, but that's only based off his record.<br><br>In the interest of being safe, and of coordinating your efforts, I thought you might want to provide some backup."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2868663351" "Infiltrate the 5th Column Base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P730319614" "It looks like Leon is still in the field. He could probably use your assistance."
// TaskTitle :
"P2805384819" "<color deepskyblue>Collateral Damage</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1410076871" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Net Victory</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2922368360" "You encountered the bodies of 5th Column guards outside the entrance to the base. It appears Leon doesn't believe in taking prisoners."
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P2538152194" "Find Leon"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3630915088" "Talk to Leon"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3383608100" "Nothing"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYINFO :
"P856364347" ""
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1511808742" "<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkgreen>Tiger 1, this is Zookeeper. Repeat, this is Zookeeper, come in Tiger 1.<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>Zookeeper, this is... ugh, I'm not playing this game anymore. What do you want, Lockhart?<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkgreen>Aww, don't be like that. I'm just calling in to let you know I'm sending you some backup.<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>No need for backup. I've just about got this in hand...<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkgreen>It's already been sent, compadre. I'm sure the two of you can mop things up nicely."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3110040087" "<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>That's a NEGATIVE, Lockhart. I've got this mission under control.<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>Extra hands will only complicate things. I'll report in as soon as I'm finished here.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkgreen>Glad to hear you're confident, Tiger 1, but Tiger 2 is already on the scene.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkgreen>You two have the same goal, so try hard not to fight."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2908867062" "<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>Laura, I'm telling you, the LAST thing I need right now is some novice tagging alo-<t=5 caption x= 0.6 y=0.3 d=5><scale 1.75><color white><bgcolor darkblue>Hold on. I'm reading nearby activity..."
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P130563127" "Leon"
// Script Variable PET_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3192765852" "Oh, it's the 'backup'. Fantastic."
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3609192693" "{HeroName}, it's you."

